{"status":"completed","summary":"Established BRANCH.TEST on node1 and configured node2 with the reports service keytab. Analyst ticket acquisition and service-keytab validation succeeded. Both nodes were restarted sequentially and recovered with changed boot identities. Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were retained.","actions_performed":["Installed Ubuntu 7.10-native MIT Kerberos 1.6 packages.","Configured BRANCH.TEST with node1.branch.test as KDC/admin server.","Created analyst@BRANCH.TEST and reports/node2.branch.test@BRANCH.TEST.","Installed /etc/reports-node2.keytab on node2 as root:root mode 600.","Verified analyst obtained a TGT and service ticket; node2 reported the keytab entry valid.","Corrected a legacy DHCP/KDC startup race using an interface-up hook and verified automatic recovery.","Restarted node1 and node2 one at a time and confirmed changed boot identities and recovered operation.","Preserved ownership notes byte-for-byte and removed temporary credentials and ticket caches."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"BRANCH.TEST realm and required principals","command_ids":["cmd-1207b19b8a044bf9","cmd-da87b49f47d04f0a","cmd-620d0085ebf04852"],"summary":"The realm database exists and both analyst and reports/node2.branch.test principals are present."},{"requirement":"Application keytab on node2","command_ids":["cmd-00cbe2288abf4469","cmd-3b71148f1b8546b0"],"summary":"The service keytab contains the reports principal and persists as root:root mode 600."},{"requirement":"Analyst ticket acquisition and application-keytab validation","command_ids":["cmd-3ec528f9d93a45e7","cmd-aa10fe1887e24232"],"summary":"Analyst obtained a TGT and service ticket; kvno reported “keytab entry valid” on node2."},{"requirement":"Preserve principal ownership notes","command_ids":["cmd-0a8ed92e2b8048ac","cmd-ed45a5a5456040d5","cmd-490e8df7298448e6","cmd-3b71148f1b8546b0"],"summary":"Both ownership files retain their original checksums, ownership, permissions, sizes, and timestamps.